WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.713
Step five reconciles.

2
00:00:01.713 --> 00:00:06.432
You give it the same register, cards,
sponsors and rules, plus an export of the

3
00:00:06.432 --> 00:00:11.762
contractor accounts in the directory, and
it reports seven findings and one warning.

4
00:00:11.762 --> 00:00:16.387
Four are C R oh one: accounts still
enabled past their earliest end.

5
00:00:16.387 --> 00:00:20.899
Those four are exactly the four disables
the middleware built in step four,

6
00:00:20.899 --> 00:00:24.975
so once those disables are sent,
the next reconciliation shows none.

7
00:00:24.975 --> 00:00:26.900
There's one orphan, C R oh two,

8
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:30.925
an enabled contractor account
with no register record.

9
00:00:30.925 --> 00:00:35.400
One C R oh three, an active card
for someone the source doesn't hold.

10
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.060
One C R oh five, a leave date
that isn't the earliest end,

11
00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:42.550
so the leaver workflow
would fire on the wrong day.

12
00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:47.138
And one warning, C R oh four, a
register record with no account.

13
00:00:47.138 --> 00:00:50.780
The reconciliation changes
nothing; it only reports.
